gin":"tetrapod00","id":145553014,"node_id":"U_kgDOCKz2dg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/145553014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00","html_url":"https://github.com/tetrapod00","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tetrapod00/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-03T04:58:51Z","updated_at":"2024-11-03T05:57:20Z","body":"From my experience it checks edits, too. Sometimes it takes a moment to propagate\r\n\r\nOn the other hand it *does not* work in comments. You can check by mousing over the word `resolves` and looking for a faint underline","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2453297452/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468882139","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98787#issuecomment-2468882139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98787","id":2468882139,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKCbb","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T19:27:40Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T19:27:40Z","body":"> Not much of a fan of too many explanation comments in code examples for miscellaneous reasons\r\n\r\nI definitely think I get what you mean and agree - this additional \"note\" is substantially longer than the actual, primary description of the method's behavior 😅 . My thought with using the X position was that it'd be a bit easier to visualize - when I found this behavior, it was with an object moving on the X axis, and once I stopped then started the tween as it was close to its target position, it was *very* clear that it was moving much slower. Using a Color's alpha may not be quite as obvious/easy to observe the behavior with. Perhaps the `X =` writing could be simplified, something like:\r\n```gdscript\r\n# Will now move from X = 250 to 500 over 1 second,\r\n```\r\nor\r\n```gdscript\r\n# Will move from 0 to 500 on the X axis over 1 second.\r\n...\r\n# Will now move from 250 to 500 over 1 second,\r\n```\r\nPerhaps we could even get rid of explicitly stating the X axis:\r\n```gdscript\r\n# Will move from 0 to 500 over 1 second.\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2468882139/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469031819","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98787#issuecomment-2469031819","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98787","id":2469031819,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TKm-L","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-11T21:14:47Z","updated_at":"2024-11-11T21:14:47Z","body":"I like the last suggestion. I think removing the explicit \"X =\" makes the example more generic but still understandable.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2469031819/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2470862859","html_url":"https://github.com/g